"Steve Leferve" <lefevre.10@osu.edu> writes:

(Running ms-dos version from ramdisk, keeping a zip on floppy)

> @echo off
> unzip nethack.zip e:
> e:/nethack.exe
> zip e:\* a:/nethack.zip

> That way, as soon as you quit nethack, it zips up the ramdive, bones files
> and all, back on to the floppy disk.

Yes.. but wouldn't that leave used bones and save files to the zip?
Either delete the zip packet before making the new one, or replace the
last zip command with something like 

zip -d -b e: a:nethack.zip  bon*.* *.sav
zip -b e: a:nethack.zip  e:bon*.* e:*.sav e:record e:logfile

That is, first remove existing bones and saves, then pack now existing
ones in, with the record and logfile.
And the -b option tells zip to use e: as the work directory for tempfiles.

